{{!-- A1, "editorial rows", on the Authors Directory: a full-width row per writer.

	{{> "directory/author-rows" authors=authors}}

	authors   the rows to render — the Directory partial owns the query

Three columns: the portrait, the biography block, and the writer's own links. Each collapses on
its own where the publication has nothing to put in it, so a writer with no photograph, no
location, no bio and no links still renders a name and a post count rather than an empty grid.

The "Latest —" line is one extra query per writer, and there is no way around it: Ghost's authors
resource carries `count.posts` and nothing about which post is newest, and Handlebars cannot join
two queries. It is an indexed `limit="1"` read against the same filter the writer's own archive
uses. A masthead is a handful of people; the 100-row cap on the Directory bounds the worst case.

That query's `filter` reads `slug` as a plain path because the loop's context IS the writer, and
its result is read through the `latest` block param rather than through the block's context —
which is what keeps this free of the `../` that {{#get}} otherwise forces.

FULL PAGE WIDTH, AND EVERY RULE ON ONE BOX. Same two corrections as directory/tag-rows.hbs, for
the same reasons: the design's 1120px override made the list start 90px inside the intro that
heads its own Surface, and a `border-t` on the `container` drew at 1320px while every row's
`border-b` — on an `article` inside the container's padding — drew at 1256px, so the list opened
with a rule wider at both ends than the rules under it. The override is gone and the top rule
moved to an inner wrapper that shares the rows' box. --}}
<section
	id="authors"
	aria-label="{{t "Writers"}}"
	class="container pt-16">
	<div class="border-border border-t">
		{{#foreach authors}}
			{{!-- Every staff account is an "author" to Ghost, so a row is drawn only for someone who
			has published. The guard is here rather than in the query because `count.posts` is not
			filterable on authors in Ghost 6 — see partials/pages/authors.hbs. --}}
			{{#if count.posts}}
				<article
					class="border-border max-stack:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] max-stack:gap-5 grid grid-cols-[96px_minmax(0,1fr)_auto] items-start gap-9 border-b py-10">
					{{> "authors/portrait" size="h-24 w-24" px="96" textSize="text-2xl" defer=true}}

					<div>
						<h2 class="font-display tracking-heading text-[32px] leading-[1.14] font-medium">
							<a
								href="{{url}}"
								class="text-text no-underline">{{name}}</a>
						</h2>

						<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-2.5 uppercase">
							{{~plural count.posts empty=(t "No posts") singular=(t "% post") plural=(t "% posts")~}}
							{{#if location}}<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>{{location}}{{/if}}
						</p>

						{{#if bio}}
							<p class="text-body text-muted mt-3.5 max-w-[60ch] leading-[1.62] text-pretty">{{bio}}</p>
						{{/if}}

						{{#get "posts" filter="authors:{{slug}}" order="published_at desc" limit="1" as |latest|}}
							{{#if latest}}
								<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-4 uppercase">
									{{~t "Latest"}} &mdash;
									{{!-- The post title keeps its underline: the design leaves this one link underlined. --}}
									<a
										href="{{latest.[0].url}}"
										class="text-text underline">{{latest.[0].title}}</a>
								</p>
							{{/if}}
						{{/get}}
					</div>

					{{!-- The third column is dropped whole where a writer published neither link, so the
					grid's 36px gap does not sit beside nothing. `{{#has any="…"}}` is Handlebars' only `or`
					here — it tests the current context for a non-empty property (`evaluateList` in
					core/frontend/helpers/has.js). --}}
					{{#has any="website,twitter"}}
						<div
							class="max-stack:items-start max-stack:flex-row max-stack:flex-wrap flex flex-col items-end gap-2">
							{{#if website}}
								<a
									href="{{website}}"
									rel="me noopener"
									class="border-border text-text font-ui rounded-sm border px-3.5 py-2 text-[13px] font-semibold whitespace-nowrap no-underline">{{readable_url website}}</a>
							{{/if}}

							{{#if twitter}}
								<a
									href="{{social_url type="twitter"}}"
									rel="me noopener"
									class="text-muted font-mono text-xs whitespace-nowrap no-underline">@{{twitter}}</a>
							{{/if}}
						</div>
					{{/has}}
				</article>
			{{/if}}
		{{/foreach}}
	</div>
</section>
